From: Dena.emu
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: sun4i-codec: turn the speaker off while headphones are plugged

On the H700 handhelds the speaker and the headphone jack both hang off
LINEOUT through an analog mux, and the headphone detect GPIO only switched
the "Headphone" DAPM pin. The "Speaker" pin stayed on, so the amplifier
(PI5) and its supply kept running next to the headphones.

On boards with a speaker amplifier GPIO, add "Speaker" to the jack pins
inverted: plugging headphones powers the speaker path down through DAPM
(which drops the amplifier GPIO and, with the 0163 patch, its supply), and
unplugging brings it back.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/sound/soc/sunxi/sun4i-codec.c
+++ b/sound/soc/sunxi/sun4i-codec.c
@@ -1623,6 +1623,16 @@ static struct snd_soc_jack_pin sun4i_headphone_jack_pins[] = {
 	{ .pin = "Headphone", .mask = SND_JACK_HEADPHONE },
 };
 
+/*
+ * Boards with a speaker amplifier: a plugged headphone also turns the
+ * speaker path off, so the amplifier and its supply power down instead of
+ * playing (or hissing) next to the headphones.
+ */
+static struct snd_soc_jack_pin sun4i_headphone_speaker_jack_pins[] = {
+	{ .pin = "Headphone", .mask = SND_JACK_HEADPHONE },
+	{ .pin = "Speaker", .mask = SND_JACK_HEADPHONE, .invert = 1 },
+};
+
 static struct snd_soc_jack_gpio sun4i_headphone_jack_gpio = {
 	.name = "hp-det",
 	.report = SND_JACK_HEADPHONE,
@@ -1636,11 +1646,18 @@ static int sun4i_codec_machine_init(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd)
 	int ret;
 
 	if (scodec->gpio_hp) {
+		struct snd_soc_jack_pin *pins = sun4i_headphone_jack_pins;
+		unsigned int num_pins = ARRAY_SIZE(sun4i_headphone_jack_pins);
+
+		if (scodec->gpio_pa) {
+			pins = sun4i_headphone_speaker_jack_pins;
+			num_pins = ARRAY_SIZE(sun4i_headphone_speaker_jack_pins);
+		}
+
 		ret = snd_soc_card_jack_new_pins(card, "Headphone Jack",
 						 SND_JACK_HEADPHONE,
 						 &sun4i_headphone_jack,
-						 sun4i_headphone_jack_pins,
-						 ARRAY_SIZE(sun4i_headphone_jack_pins));
+						 pins, num_pins);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err(rtd->dev,
 				"Headphone jack creation failed: %d\n", ret);
